{
 "schema": 1,
 "about": "The three ways this repo ranks a batch count (KernelCost's model, #54; the wall-clock recommendation, #56; the counters' ridge crossing, #112/#114) read against each other per (L, arch) of measured.SUBGRID (felizjueves.crossread, #115). The choice is the clock's, everywhere: Measured outranks Cost. Every disagreement is a StructuralLimit in data/measured/limits.json. An order, never a prediction. Recomputed by test/test_kernelrank.py.",
 "header": {
  "model": "kernelrank.model_cell(spec, kernelrank.BUDGET[arch]).traffic_sum: KernelCost.traffic summed over the batch kernels (#54's headline). order = batch counts grouped by value, ascending; pick = the first group (ties kept).",
  "clock": "batchreport.recommend: best median per input, with resolved and within_spread as #56 defines them.",
  "counters": "ridge.crossing, both variants (#114's declared rule); first_compute_bound = 1 if compute-bound already at 1 batch, the crossing count if crossed, null if never. The counter run is the WIDE-T input only, so clock.wide is the same-input comparison and clock.near is not.",
  "choice": "The clock's best per input, and only that: Measured outranks Cost. The model and the counters choose nothing.",
  "agree": "model_clock: clock best in model pick. clock_crossing: clock best == first compute-bound count. model_crossing: first compute-bound count in model pick. null = the card could not be measured (measured_store.UNMEASURED): an absence, not a disagreement.",
  "small_sample": "4 L x 2 cards x 5 batch counts. Each cell reports which count each instrument names, never a prediction interval or a pooled score.",
  "disagreements": "Each is covered by a StructuralLimit in data/measured/limits.json whose asserted_value has cross_read = true.",
  "regenerate": "PYTHONPATH=src uv run python -m felizjueves.crossread --write"
 },
